# Lab 01: Introduction to Basic Logic Gates

## Objective
To study and verify the truth tables of basic logic gates: AND, OR, NOT, NAND, and NOR.

## Theory & Truth Tables

### 1. AND Gate
The AND gate produces a HIGH (1) output only when all of its inputs are HIGH.


### 2. OR Gate
The OR gate produces a HIGH (1) output if at least one of its inputs is HIGH.



### 3. NOT Gate (Inverter)
The NOT gate produces an output that is the exact opposite (complement) of its input.



### 4. NAND Gate (Universal Gate)
The NAND gate is the complement of the AND gate. It produces a LOW (0) output only when all inputs are HIGH.



### 5. NOR Gate (Universal Gate)
The NOR gate is the complement of the OR gate. It produces a HIGH (1) output only when all inputs are LOW.


I have successfully verified the truth tables and outputs of all the basic logic gates.
